WHY THE CALL SITE IS HERE AND NOT EARLIER
-----------------------------------------
Placing it after `would_cross` is deliberate. A quote that would breach
post-only must still be cancelled regardless of how far behind the bid it
sits, and `would_cross` is the check that decides that. Placing the new call
before it would let the tolerance keep a crossing quote alive.

Placing it inside the `touch != px_` branch rather than replacing that branch
is also deliberate: when the quote IS at the touch the branch never fires, so
there is nothing to decide, and leaving the condition alone keeps the diff to
an insertion.

